<article class="env-definition" id="01AM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01AM">Definition <span data-tag="01AM">17.4.1</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. We say that $\mathcal{F}$ is <em>generated by global sections</em> if there exist a set $I$, and global sections $s_ i \in \Gamma (X, \mathcal{F})$, $i \in I$ such that the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bigoplus \nolimits _{i \in I} \mathcal{O}_ X \longrightarrow \mathcal{F}  \]
</div>
  <p> which is the map associated to $s_ i$ on the summand corresponding to $i$, is surjective. In this case we say that the sections $s_ i$ <em>generate</em> $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article>